# Simple

## Reality

- Finch accepts small diagnostic uploads from one internal client.
- Live deployment, account, device and distribution state are not available here.

## Preserve

- Public privacy claims must match retained payload behavior.

## Current boundary

- Source and local evidence can be audited; unavailable live state remains unknown.

## Ordinary paths

- README owns public claims, accepted decisions own retention, and scripts own release verification.

## Proof

- Use repository evidence and read-only checks. Do not claim live proof.

## Reconsider when

- Reassess deployed identity only with an authenticated live response or account object.
